            "review_title": "Review at Kichi Kichi Vincom",
            "review_text": "AKflyboy\nDubai, United Arab Emirates137 contributions\n0\nEat Thyself Silly\nDec 2015 • Friends\nHere in the land of small portions and small people, there are few places where a full-sized, active, American male can consume the needed quantities of meat for reasonable coinage. This is one. There's nothing particularly upscale about Kichi, but it is clean, consistent, and delivers a nice hot-pot experience you'll want to return to. Ok, let's just get to the point. Who won't become a fan of food being delivered continuously and quickly on a conveyor belt? Seafood, sushi, fresh udon noodles, vegetables, mushrooms....BEEF... elbow to elbow with 100 of your closest friends all enjoying personal hotpot at it's finest. \n\nSpeaking of that, beat the lunch or dinner rush by a half-hour or you're likely to find the place crowded. Never had to wait for a seat, but if you want to pick your position before the action heats up....you get the idea. \n\nAll told, maybe it is hotpot served fast food style. But it's a clever arrangement that works. Go try. You'll find out why I signed up for the membership card.\nRead more\nWritten December 31, 2015",
